      "text": "Now, we can assume that all three paths P(vu,uv), P(vw,wv), P(uw,wu) are pairwise at distance at least K. In this case, we can build a K-fat K3-minor in G. Set Hv := G[DG(v,⌊32K⌋)], Hu := G[DG(u,⌊32K⌋)], Hw := G[DG(w,⌊32K⌋)]. It is easy to see that these connected subgraphs Hv,Hw,Hu and paths P(vu,uv), P(vw,wv), P(uw,wu) form a K-fat K3minor in G. Recall that dG(v,P(u,w)) ≥ 4K, dG(u,P(v,w)) ≥ 4K and dG(w,P(u,v)) ≥ 4K. Hence, if dG(V (Hv),V (Hu)) < K, then dG(v,u) < ⌊23K⌋ + K + ⌊23K⌋ ≤ 4K, which is impossible. If dG(V (Hv),P(uw,wu)) < K, then dG(v,P(u,w)) < ⌊32K⌋ + K < 3K, which is also impossible. By symmetries, the K3-minor constructed is K-fat. ⊔⊓",
