      "text": "Note that, in the proof of Lemma 12, we constructed very speciﬁc K-fat (K3,K1,3)-minors. In our K-fat K3-minor, the connected subgraphs H1,H2,H3 are disks. In our K-fat K1,3minor, the connected subgraphs H1,H2,H3 are singletons and the paths Pi,0, i = 1,2,3, are shortest paths. Even more speciﬁc K-fat (K3,K1,3)-minors were obtained in [1]. It was shown that if a graph G contains no (≥ K)-subdivision of K3 as a geodesic subgraph and no (≥ 3K)subdivision of K1,3 as a 3-quasi-geodesic subgraph, then pb(G) ≤ 18K + 2 (see [1] for details and deﬁnitions).",
